    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Frequency and duration of unplanned generation outages reduced completely by March 2017. 
Progress/Status: As of May 2018, unplanned generation outages have been eliminated completely. All current outages are considered planned for maintenance purposes.
As of December 2017, the average outage duration (SAIDI) has dropped to about 2 days a year from 47 days in 2015, and average number of interruptions (SAIFI) dropped to 1 outage every 8 days from 1.3 outages every day in 2015. 
Data Source: NUC service logs 
Actual value:</narrative>
